Error [jet.MoveWithoutMarker]: `finish` takes `machine`, but `machine` is used again later
  --> tests/ui/move_fallback_diverging.jet:42:21
    |
 42 |         _ := finish(machine, false)
    |                     ^^^^^^^
  --> tests/ui/move_fallback_diverging.jet:45:12
    |
 45 |     finish(machine, first > 0)
    |            ^^^^^^^ `machine` is used again here
 Why: `finish` takes ownership of this argument, and a call never copies on its own, so `machine` has no value after this call
 Fix: Write `machine.copy()` to pass a copy and keep `machine`, or reorder so this call is the last use of `machine`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0209
